From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:22:14 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Arm64EC: Emulate x86 execute breakpoints (Dr0-Dr3).

PACE's anti-tamper code (iLok-protected plugins such as Neural DSP's) sets Dr0-Dr3 on its own
thread with SetThreadContext and expects EXCEPTION_SINGLE_STEP each time a probe address runs,
with Dr6 = 0xffff0ff0 | the slots that hit. Under ARM64EC the debug registers were dropped, the
probes never trapped and the plugin failed later with c0000409.

Wine's ARM64 context has no room for the x64 debug registers, so Wine's ARM64EC
NtSetContextThread, NtContinue(Ex) and NtGetContextThread pass them to the new exports
SetThreadDebugContext and GetThreadDebugContext (vstbridge's wine-fex patch). FEX keeps them per
thread, adds enabled execute breakpoints (R/W=00) to a process-wide address set and invalidates
code compiled there. Before an instruction at an address in the set, the JIT compares it with
the thread's breakpoints and raises #DB (TRAP_HWBKPT) on a hit, unless the resume flag (RF) skips
it once. The exception context reports Dr0-Dr3, Dr6, Dr7 and RF as x86 Linux and Windows do,
and single steps report Dr6 with BS. Code with no breakpoints compiles as before; pages with
breakpoints bypass the disk cache. Data breakpoints aren't emulated.
